WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.770
- Well, tell us about
your time in the military.

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.690
You served for, was it nearly 17 years?

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:05.760
- 17 and a half total time in service.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.000
I had 10 and a half active duty.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.250
(audience cheers, applauds)
- Oh, wow.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:11.820
- But yeah, I was with the
82nd Airborne, the 101st.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.140
Had the great privilege of working

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:14.850
with some of the greatest
people in the world.

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:17.370
- Yeah, wow, well, so
even though you're retired

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:18.900
from the military, you say
that that training kinda

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.010
never goes away, right?

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:21.750
- That's a fact, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.310
- I say this from my stage every night

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:26.100
when we're on stage, and I
use the term once a soldier,

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.410
always a soldier, and it is the truth.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:29.460
- Yeah.
- It's just something

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:32.460
that never gets away from you.
- Yeah.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.170
- All of these people can attest that.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:35.850
No matter what they do
in their future lives,

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.160
wherever they may end up,
what they're doing right now

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.710
will be with them forever,
and those relationships,

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:42.570
which is also a wonderful thing.

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:44.790
- Yeah!
- They never go away.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:45.810
- I hope not for them.

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:47.880
So you're very popular with the military.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:48.900
I'm sure they connect with you

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.550
because obviously,
you're a veteran as well,

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.890
but why do you think your
songs hit them so deeply?

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:54.360
'Cause people love you.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:55.557
- I wished I knew.

00:00:55.557 --> 00:00:56.390
(both laughing)

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:58.080
- Then you'd know the secret. (laughs)

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.668
- I think it's because I sing and write

00:01:00.668 --> 00:01:02.940
from their perspective, really.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:03.840
- Yeah.
- I mean,

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.040
like I said, I'm a soldier.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.570
I entertain people now.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:08.730
I sing, and I write
songs, produce records,

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:10.560
get to be in movies, which is why I'm.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:11.983
For the record, any of you.

00:01:11.983 --> 00:01:13.770
- I love this!
- People making fun of this,

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:17.250
thinking I'm not clean-shaven
like I normally am.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:21.180
Like I said, I think it's
because I'm still them,

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.790
and like you, we're still fans.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:25.200
- Yeah.
- So when I sing and write,

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.910
I try to sing from that perspective,

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:28.560
as if I wanted to hear the song.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.290
- Absolutely; sometimes
I write to something

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:32.790
that I wanna hear that'll
help me kinda heal,

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:33.623
and that's why I do it.

00:01:33.623 --> 00:01:34.593
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

